<h1>TActiveImage</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.1" />
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.ActiveControls.TActiveImage" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TActiveImage</tt> is the active control counterpart of
<a href="?page=Controls.Image">TImage</a>. It renders an <tt>&lt;img&gt;</tt> element in
the same way and adds the ability to change its attributes during a callback.
</p>

<h2>What updates during a callback</h2>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Property</th><th>Attribute rewritten</th></tr>
<tr><td><tt>ImageUrl</tt></td><td><tt>src</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>AlternateText</tt></td><td><tt>alt</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>ImageAlign</tt></td><td><tt>align</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>DescriptionUrl</tt></td><td><tt>longdesc</tt></td></tr>
</table>

<p class="block-content">
Each update is subject to <a href="?page=ActiveControls.Introduction#ClientSideUpdates">the five conditions for a client-side update</a>. Swapping <tt>ImageUrl</tt> is the common
case, and changing <tt>AlternateText</tt> with it keeps the new image described.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>ImageAlign</tt> and <tt>DescriptionUrl</tt> are inherited from <tt>TImage</tt> and
both are deprecated, because HTML5 dropped the attributes they write. Use the CSS
<tt>float</tt> or <tt>vertical-align</tt> declaration and an ARIA attribute such as
<tt>aria-describedby</tt> instead.
</p>
